        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Pydna</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">22 June 168 BCE; the fighting began in the afternoon</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">A fairly level plain near Katerini, a village south of Pydna, below the foothills of Mount Olocrus in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-roman-province">Macedonia</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and its allies under the consul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-aemilius-paullus-macedonicus">Lucius Aemilius Paullus</a>, at least 28,600 men and up to 37,000; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perseus-of-macedon">Perseus</a>, 43,000 soldiers at the start of the war and closer to 30,000 by the time of the battle</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-legion">Roman legions</a> broke the Macedonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phalanx">phalanx</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perseus-of-macedon">Perseus</a> fled, nearly 11,000 Macedonians were captured, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a> reported that his sources claimed up to 20,000 Macedonian dead.</span></div>
        </div>
