    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> fought with two legions in the centre and allied infantry on the flanks, and the Macedonians with a pike <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phalanx">phalanx</a> and an elite guard of 3,000.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phalanx">phalanx</a> lost its cohesion as it advanced over rough ground in the foothills, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-aemilius-paullus-macedonicus">Paullus</a> ordered the legions into the gaps to attack the phalangites on their exposed flanks.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perseus-of-macedon">Perseus</a> was later paraded in triumph in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in chains, the Macedonian kingdom was dissolved into four republics, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-roman-province">Macedonia</a> in time became a Roman province.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The night before the battle there was a lunar eclipse, which the Macedonians perceived as an ill omen; according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plutarch">Plutarch</a>, they took it as a sign of their king's demise.</p></aside>
    </section>

